        "text": "Around 960 AD, Harald Bluetooth Gormsson, a king who united Denmark and Norway, introduced Christianity to the Danes. His conversion is traditionally linked to the missionary Poppo. Harald explicitly detailed his conversion and role in Christianizing the Danes on the Jelling stones, erected during his reign.",
